From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:14:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: fire the Bukkit teleport events Folia left
 unimplemented

Two hooks in Entity, both at points upstream already marks as event territory.

teleportAsync: fire PlayerTeleportEvent (players) or EntityTeleportEvent
(everything else) just above the destination unload lock. That is after all the
validity checks and before anything is mutated, so a cancel is a plain return
false - the same answer teleportAsync already gives for its own refusals - with
no lock to unwind, and it sits above the same-region/cross-region branch so one
hook covers same region, cross region and cross world. The thread is right by
construction: teleportAsync opens with TickThread.ensureTickThread on this
entity, so the handler runs on the region that owns it. Nothing blocks, nothing
waits on another region, no ownership check is touched. A handler that redirects
via setTo is honoured, including to another world.

placeInAsync: fire PlayerChangedWorldEvent from the completion that runs on the
destination region, once the entity has actually been placed - guarded on the
world really having changed, because placeInAsync also handles same-world cross
-region moves. It goes before teleportComplete because that callback releases
the destination's unload read lock.

Teleports whose cause is UNKNOWN are skipped: that is what Folia and Luminol
pass for internal repositioning with no Paper counterpart (fixPassengerDesync,
guardEntityTick's out-of-region recovery) and what TamableAnimal passes after
having already fired EntityTeleportEvent itself. Everything with a real cause is
a teleport Paper would also have reported, and no Bukkit API overload produces
UNKNOWN by default.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.teleportEvents=false

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
index ef8f41f05255de25b5f831275bd1e5e1340f6141..c6cff434e2b73bb35a031d46e8f59b4d9017237d 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java
@@ -4407,6 +4407,17 @@ public abstract class Entity
                         node.root.postChangeDimension();
                     }
 
+                    // Lophinya start - PlayerChangedWorldEvent; placeInAsync also runs for same-world
+                    // cross-region moves, so the world really has to have changed. Fired before
+                    // teleportComplete because that callback releases the destination's unload read
+                    // lock, and the handler should still be covered by it.
+                    if (originWorld != destination && fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaTeleportEvents.ENABLED) {
+                        for (EntityTreeNode node : fullTree) {
+                            fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaTeleportEvents.callChangedWorld(node.root, originWorld);
+                        }
+                    }
+                    // Lophinya end
+
                     if (teleportComplete != null) {
                         teleportComplete.accept(Entity.this);
                     }
@@ -4570,12 +4581,29 @@ public abstract class Entity
             }
         }
 
+        // Lophinya start - fire the Bukkit teleport events Folia left as a TODO below
+        // Deliberately above the unload lock: a cancel here is a plain return, with no lock to
+        // unwind and nothing mutated yet. See LophinyaTeleportEvents for the full rationale.
+        if (fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaTeleportEvents.ENABLED) {
+            final fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaTeleportEvents.Destination lophinyaDestination =
+                fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaTeleportEvents.callTeleportEvent(this, destination, pos, yaw, pitch, cause);
+            if (lophinyaDestination == null) {
+                return false;
+            }
+            destination = lophinyaDestination.level();
+            pos = lophinyaDestination.pos();
+            yaw = lophinyaDestination.yaw();
+            pitch = lophinyaDestination.pitch();
+        }
+        // Lophinya end
+
         // Luminol start - Level hot unload apis
         if (!destination.levelUnloadStateLock.acquireRead()) {
             return false;
         }
+        final ServerLevel finalDestination = destination; // Lophinya - the event may have redirected it, and the lambda below needs an effectively final capture
         final java.util.function.Consumer<Entity> finalTeleportComplete = entity -> {
-            destination.levelUnloadStateLock.releaseRead();
+            finalDestination.levelUnloadStateLock.releaseRead(); // Lophinya - was destination, which is no longer effectively final
 
             if (teleportComplete != null) teleportComplete.accept(entity);
         };
